Gaspode wrote:

> Last night while playing I accidently stumbled upon a hidden stash on a
> level and at first I wasn't quite sure what had happened.  Apparently I
> had found a 1x1 room and while searching I was teleported to the stash.

The unconnected 2x2 room with the gold is a vault. Many (nor all) levels
have them.

>  I picked up all of the gold, and then a guard appeared and told me to
> leave the money and then follow him out.  Besides teleportation is
> there a way to get out.  

Dig through the wall or through the floor. Level teleport or cursed potion
of gain level. Poly into something that can eat or walk through rock.

If you want to stay in the vault (for instance because you're waiting
until your teleportitis kicks in) when the guard comes, you can tell him
that you're the boss of all the vaults, the richest man in history, by
his Latin, Greek or Discworld spelling.

> It seems that killing the guard may be a bad 
> idea as he leads you out.  

Yes, especially as they're peaceful as long as you don't attack them.

> Is this why you see the "You hear a guard 
> muttering" message?  

"You hear the footsteps of a guard on patrol". That's one of the messages
that indicate that there is a vault on the level. There's also "You hear
someone counting money" and when hallucinating "You hear Ebenezer
Scrooge".

> Are these 1x1 rooms that seem to appear fairly 
> often used for anything else?

There are also empty closets, closets with level teleporters and closets
with trap doors. The empty ones have no writing in front of the door;
those with level teleporters the same as the vault teleporters (so
beware); those with trap doors a different message.

